 "_doc": "Overworld light, weather look, screen effects and map transitions per era (EraLight, EraLightLayer). A map uses the era of its own region, never a newer one than the active era, so old regions keep their origin look. Era I: no day tint, weather as a flat ink pattern plus one text line, cut or plain fade between maps, caves one ink darker with a small light circle. Era II: three tints (morning, day, night), lit windows, plain rain lines. Era III: four tints, rain with splashes and puddles, sandstorm, ash fall, fog bands, lightning, door and stairs wipes. Era IV: light shafts under trees, lamp glow, snow that keeps prints, cloud shadows. Era V: smooth light over the hours with a golden hour, long shadows, season tint per region, leaves, pollen and embers, a camera sweep into big places. Booleans only ever switch on in later eras (GUT test). flash: lightning is capped in code at 3 flashes per second whatever this file says and is off under reduced motion.",
